  "scopeNotes": [
    "Common UI uses Vector2 pixel coordinates regardless of world dimension.",
    "Shared DamageNumber class moved to common-damage-numbers.md; pool remains 2d-damage-numbers.md. Tests extracting class_name DamageNumber need common source.",
    "Hitbox/Hurtbox class blocks moved from component-system/SKILL.md into 2d-hitboxes.md; new 3D classes are suffixed 3D.",
    "Existing C# DamageNumber selection: common-damage-numbers.md block 0. DamageNumberSpawner selection: 2d-damage-numbers.md block 0 (previously block 1).",
    "New engine suite: tests/godot-examples/cases/dimensions-gameplay.mjs, 4 passing cases. New C# compile selections: work/dimension-gameplay-csharp.json, 17 additions validated with 2 actual shared dependencies.",
    "Scope API checks used Godot 4.7.2 runtime, official GodotSharp 4.7.2 XML, and official Camera3D/AudioStreamPlayer2D/AudioStreamPlayer3D documentation.",
    "Six shared entry SKILL.md files keep discovery IDs and use (Common) titles; reference names and routing identify 2D/3D/common.",
    "Common FSM entity type is Node, with typed CharacterState2D/3D adapters; lifecycle tests continue to use the same State/StateMachine implementation.",
    "Input device, cursor and scalar curve APIs stay common; Vector2 screen or graph coordinates do not imply a 2D-only game feature.",
    "First-person look/SpringArm collision are 3D-specific; 2D camera framing uses follow, limits and planar orbit. 3D room zones select cameras rather than invent Camera2D limit properties.",
    "3D ground examples use XZ movement, Y gravity, world-unit thresholds; flying volumetric navigation is explicitly excluded from ground navmesh examples.",
    "Split screen shares one level World2D/World3D instead of duplicating physics worlds.",
    "New runtime cases: dimensions-movement.mjs verifies XY/XZ direction, analog magnitude, deadzone overshoot, gravity signs, typed FSM owner, and navigation horizontal stop preserving falling velocity. Additional recipes imported against Godot 4.7.2.",
    "C# State selection moved from block1 to block0 in state-machine/SKILL.md; enums moved into 2d/3d-enum-enemy refs.",
    "Common ActionBuffer now separates event buffering from body movement and has expiration/consume-once runtime checks.",
    "Dedicated-server configuration, lobby, match flow and deployment are dimension independent.",
    "Common RPC intro now uses Node and chat only; typed position RPCs moved to paired authority movement recipes.",
    "Prediction examples use a bounded fixed-step replay core and explicitly document transport and collision integration limits.",
    "Lag compensation now uses dimension-consistent vector types and finite rays against copied, bounded historical circle/sphere snapshots.",
    "Shared bandwidth guide delegates authority-side distance filtering and nearest-viewer rate selection to paired interest-management recipes.",
    "Jolt and SoftBody3D remain 3D-only; one-way CollisionShape2D is 2D-only.",
    "2D ragdolls use jointed RigidBody2D parts; they do not invent PhysicalBoneSimulator2D.",
    "Physics Camera2D samples physics positions because the interpolated-global-transform getter is Node3D-only.",
    "BSP/cave 3D counterparts build planar XZ GridMap levels; volumetric density uses get_noise_3d. WFC remains a shared planar constraint algorithm and explicitly does not claim volumetric coverage.",
    "Optimization now separates concrete 2D/3D rendering and pool placement, retaining profiling/memory/core pool behavior in common references. Removed unsafe offscreen-collider pooling and false CanvasGroup/GC claims in touched examples.",
    "39 new or updated C# class selections compiled with official Godot.NET.Sdk 4.7.2; no errors or warnings.",
    "Four dimensions-physics engine tests passed, including actual 2D clockwise/3D negative-Y right steering, physics overlap, connected BSP floors, detached pool lifetime, and MultiMesh transform arguments.",
    "Common animation combo now extends Node; hit feedback split by rendering node.",
    "Subemitters remain common with complete 2D and 3D blocks; target path belongs to emitter node, not process material.",
    "Turbulence moved from 3D-only attractor reference to shared process-material reference.",
    "Control/Label HUD tween recipes remain common; transform tweens have dimensional references.",
    "3D skeleton modifier/IK APIs, glTF humanoid retargeting, volumetric fog, GI, mesh LOD, and compositor remain 3D-specific. Skeleton2D cutout reference is the actual 2D skeletal approach, not suffix-swapped 3D IK.",
    "3D perspective supplies parallax; 2D parallax scroll, terrain autotiling, and pixel snapping remain dimension-specific.",
    "Stencil docs corrected to spatial-only stencil_mode syntax; alpha texture masking supplies the 2D gameplay counterpart.",
    "Headless checks cover engine behavior and configuration, not GPU appearance."
  ]
}
